diff --git a/tools/server/README.md b/tools/server/README.md
index ef9033404..656a0268f 100644
--- a/tools/server/README.md
+++ b/tools/server/README.md
@@ -929,7 +929,49 @@ To use this endpoint with POST method, you need to start server with `--props`
 
 *Options:*
 
-- None yet
+- `parallel` (int): number of slots that accept new requests, 1 to the `--parallel` value at startup. Slots taken out of service are cleared and skipped when a slot is picked for a new request.
+- `ctx_per_slot` (int): per-request context ceiling, i.e. how many tokens a single request may use. Requires `--kv-unified` (see below).
+- `allow_oversubscribe` (bool, default `false`): allow `parallel * ctx_per_slot` to exceed the KV pool. Without it such a request is rejected with the arithmetic in the error message.
+- `ctx` (int): total KV pool, i.e. the `-c` value. Recreates the `llama_context`.
+- `cache_type_k`, `cache_type_v` (string): same values as `--cache-type-k` / `--cache-type-v`. Recreates the `llama_context`.
+- `flash_attn` (string): `on`, `off` or `auto`. Recreates the `llama_context`.
+- `parallel_max` (int): number of slots to create, i.e. the `--parallel` value. Recreates the `llama_context`.
+- `kv_unified` (bool): turn the shared KV pool on or off. Recreates the `llama_context`.
+- `rebuild` (bool): force a context recreation even if only the keys above are given.
+
+Two groups of properties behave differently:
+
+**Slot policy (`parallel`, `ctx_per_slot`) is applied in place.** These need no context recreation, so they are immediate: no reload, no VRAM change, in-flight requests are unaffected and existing prompts stay in the KV cache of the slots that remain in service. This works when the server runs with `--kv-unified`, because then the whole `-c` window is one pool shared by the slots, and the split between them is server-side policy. Per-slot ceiling changes apply to the next admitted prompt.
+
+```sh
+# shrink the window from 4 x 64k to 2 x 128k on the same pool, without touching the weights
+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/props -d '{"parallel":2,"ctx_per_slot":131072}'
+```
+
+Without `--kv-unified` the `-c` window is divided between the slots when the KV cache is created
+(`n_ctx_seq = n_ctx / n_seq_max`), so the split cannot change at runtime and these calls are rejected with
+an explanation. Restart with `--kv-unified`, or use the rebuild keys below.
+
+**Context properties (`ctx`, `cache_type_*`, `flash_attn`, `parallel_max`, `kv_unified`) recreate the
+`llama_context`.** The model weights are not reloaded and stay where they are (VRAM or RAM), so this is
+much cheaper than restarting the server, but the KV cache and the prompt state are dropped and the call
+is only applied once no request is being decoded. If the new context cannot be created (e.g. it does not
+fit in VRAM) the previous one is restored and the call reports the failure.
+
+```sh
+# double the pool and switch the V cache to f16, weights stay in VRAM
+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/props -d '{"ctx":262144,"cache_type_v":"f16"}'
+```
+
+The response echoes the configuration that is now in effect, e.g.
+```json
+{"success":true,"slots":2,"slots_max":8,"ctx_per_slot":131072,"kv_unified":true,"kv_pool_n_ctx":262144}
+```
+and `GET /props` reports `total_slots` (slots in service), `slots_max` (slots created), `kv_unified`,
+`kv_unified_per_slot` and `kv_pool_n_ctx`.
+
+Note: `parallel_max` and `kv_unified` cannot be applied by the slot policy, and a multimodal server
+(`--mmproj`) does not support the rebuild path.
 
 ### POST `/embeddings`: non-OpenAI-compatible embeddings API
 
